Wow, this one was hard, otherwise I wouldn't post.

Delmer the vegetarian elf ascended with coming up on 4 million 
points last night after a very rocky journey.

As the game's been a bit uneventful for me recently, I decided to 
set myself a few rules this time to make it interesting. I let 
the game choose my class each time, and rejected all the hack-and 
slash characters. After that, I took whatever I got and played it 
vegetarian. I decided rings weren't vegetables, too.

I died a _lot_.

The biggest troubles I had with Delmer the Elf were encumbrance 
(I had to carry all my food with me), lack of easy T-porting, 
Gold Nagas, Black Dragons, and lack of various resistances. It 
also took him a long time to get ESP.

Black Dragons almost punched my ticket in Ft. Ludios. I don't 
think I've ever approached the damn things without appropriate 
resistances or reflection. I emptied a wand of cancellation and a 
wand of undead turning before I got some scales. I also lost most 
of my armor, including a +4 dented pot :(

Kudos to the guy who came up with the undead turning trick, BTW. 
Clever, that.

Did some polypiling and used up a marker after that to get my AC 
down in the -30 range. Polypiling was the only thing that kept me 
alive, this game. I know it's naughty, but I can't help myself :)

I was very lucky with enchanting this game for some reason. I 
regularly ended up with +5 armor, and I even got Grayswandir up 
to +7 after I found it (cursed!) in a bones file.

Anyway, I lost most of my armor, including +2 BDSM, +5 Helm of 
Brilliance, +3 Cloak of Protection, and +2 Speed boots, to Gold 
Nagas on the castle level. I would have bought it right there 
without my handy-dandy ring of conflict, which I hadn't used 
until then.

I promptly genocided the slimy bastards, wished for GDSM, and 
polypiled until I got an amulet of reflection.

After that it was a bit of a cakewalk as usual. The Wiz gave me a 
bit of trouble in one or two places because I always seemed to be 
without a quick kill, but he didn't put in much of a showing. I 
suppose I didn't give him much opportunity; you can get out of 
the dungeon pretty fast when you're chaotic.

Here's a tip; tame lots of cockatrices. If they're fast and 
invisible, they clean out the wiz's pets, and when they get 
killed, you've got an UDW on hand. The Elf's quest item gives you 
free taming, so I played the ablative pet game a lot.

That's about it. Early on I dropped my gems for encumbrance 
considerations, and I forgot to pick them up on the way out, so 
my score wasn't as high as it could be. I managed to pad it a bit 
with the gems from the ascended heroes on the Astral Plane, tho.

I'm going to get some work done, now. I erased the damn program 
off my HD last night!

Of course, I still have the nh313386.exe file on floppy 
somewhere . . .
